    <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, come on. It wasn’t that bad!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kohler</span> laughs, though you’re pretty sure that box of papers weighed just as much as you do! <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Fair, fair.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kohler</span> chuckles, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on, just need to take this stuff back to my office. It isn’t anywhere near as heavy!”</span> He tosses one of the boxes to you and you groan. <span style="color:Yellow">Sure, it isn’t AS heavy, but it is still pretty heavy.</span> <br>
    <<needChange "Energy" -5>>
    <br>
    As you begin to walk back down the stairs, you ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kohler</span> about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span>. What was he doing in the gym? <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span>? Oh, yeah. He does martial arts training on the weekend and asked if he could practice after class on the days I don’t host detention. The kid’s pretty dedicated and not half bad either, though he gets a little flustered if anyone watches him.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kohler</span> chuckles as you walk back into the locker room and carry the last box into his office. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Right, now run along. If you’re still here when I start locking up, maybe I will host a detention today.”</span> You blush and nod, hurrying out of his office back into the locker room when something catches your eye. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:Pink">You spot <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span>’s gym clothes on the ground and hear the shower going. He must have finished his work out and is getting ready to leave.</span> You pause for a moment, thinking about what you’ve learned about him. You have a lot of questions, though guess you just haven’t found the right time to ask since you’ve technically only just met him. You are about to leave when you hear the water stop and wet footsteps approaching! You quickly step back, slightly out of sight, and walk as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span> walks past towards his locker, <span style="color:Pink">his small body wrapped in only a towel.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <<art "Images\\Special\\Buyable\\OC\\Kade\\Kade Towel.png" "Rayray" "https:rayray.fanbox.cc" 700>>

    <span style="color:LightGreen">That’s when you realize the boy is ripped! He’s not the skinny little kid he appeared in the hallway, but rather is rocking some well-defined muscles, ones that would give even someone like <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> a run for their money.</span> You can’t believe it and find yourself staring as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span> stands only a few feet in front of you, back to you as he stretches his arms into the air. <br>
    <br>
    But then you also notice something else, something that makes you second-guess saying or doing anything to him. <span style="color:LightCoral">Scars, old ones possibly, across his back in harsh lines. Are they from an old accident or injury? Maybe that’s why he likes to stay late, so he doesn’t have to shower and change in front of everyone else.</span> A few thoughts linger in your mind, though you quickly shake them off, instead focusing just on the small, yet surprisingly muscular boy in front of you. <br>
    <br>
    You’ve been standing here for so long, you should say or do something, or else this will become a very awkward encounter. <span style="color:Yellow">But what should you do to break the ice? That towel looks awfully lose on him, but you get the feeling he’d be very mad if you suddenly yanked it off him.</span> <br>
    <br>
