                <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“T- thanks again, for earlier I mean. When you helped me after…”</span> He pauses, sounding very nervous. You smile and tell him it was no problem, though admit you have a question. Why did he let those kids walk all over him? You saw him in the gym practicing, he could have easily whooped their butts. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I-”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span> gives a nervous half-smile at your words, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t like violence. I like practicing and performing and all that, b- but I don’t want to use it against people.”</span> <br>
                <br>
                You guess you understand that but still feel bad about those kids picking on him. If he even showed a little of what he can do, they’d leave him alone for sure! <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s fine… really…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">looks up at you and gives you a larger smile,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“B- but… thank you. I’m glad you thought I was good.”</span> You return his smile and chat with him for a bit, asking questions about his skills and training. He happily answers them, <span style="color:Pink">though things are still a little awkward since he is dripping wet in just a towel.</span> <br>
                <br>
                So, you bid farewell to the boy, asking if you could pick up your conversation another time. <span style="color:LightGreen">He happily agrees, happy that you decided to talk with him despite the awkward situation. You walk off feeling you’ve made a new friend.</span> <br>
