                <span style="color:Yellow">The silence and awkwardness between you two are thick, the weight of your earlier bullying of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span> lingering in the air.</span> So, you finally come out and say it. You apologize for earlier, saying that smacking his butt like that wasn’t right and you would have deserved him throwing a punch or a kick your way. <br>
                <br>
                <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“O- oh…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span> looks up at you, seemingly surprised that you’re saying sorry. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It- it’s fine. It happens… and I don’t like violence, so I wouldn’t have…”</span> He pauses, staring at his feet for a second before looking up and <span style="color:LightGreen">giving a nervous smile.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I- I forgive you. M- my name is <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span>, but I guess you know that. It’s nice to meet you – properly – I mean.”</span> The boy is a little awkward, but seems to be trying his best to come off as friendly. <span style="color:LightGreen">You return his smile, happy to be forgiven, and chat with him for a bit, asking questions about his skills and training.</span> <span style="color:Pink">He happily answers them, though things are still a little awkward since he is dripping wet in just a towel.</span> <br>
